      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how Grimoire\u0027s guarded write mechanism prevents partial failures during file operations. \n\nIn brief, it works like this: before any file is overwritten, the guarded write executor first records the file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist yet\u2014into an in-memory journal. If the agent run subsequently fails (due to hitting a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied write attempts), that journal can roll all the recorded writes back in reverse order: restoring old content where files existed before, or deleting newly created files. This provides all-or-nothing semantics for the entire run\u0027s write operations without needing a traditional database transaction.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent doesn\u0027t actually use this rollback functionality since it has no write capability at all, though the journal type itself is part of the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5344,
      "output_tokens": 196
    }
